2
00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:01.860
Yes. Mr. Cho.

3
00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:04.099
Yes. that's the place.

4
00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:10.340
The warehouse where

5
00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:12.289
we worked on the Japanese kid.

6
00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:16.900
Yes. he's comfy and well.

7
00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:19.970
He was a lot more gentle
than what you told me.

8
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:26.180
He wasn't trouble at all.
he took my lead well.

9
00:01:27.039 --> 00:01:28.870
He was a bit cheeky though.

10
00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:31.880
He's a funny guy.

11
00:01:36.259 --> 00:01:40.130
How much was this guy worth
by the way?

12
00:01:47.039 --> 00:01:50.020
Right? I knew he was loaded.

13
00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:53.890
He's covered in designer goods.
He must be well off.

14
00:01:56.229 --> 00:01:57.229
What?

15
00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.390
Oh...

16
00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.870
He must be rich.

17
00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:09.460
Yes. I see.

18
00:02:09.539 --> 00:02:12.610
We got proper merchandise
for once.

19
00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:19.920
Almost here? I left the door open.

20
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.380
Come on right in.

21
00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:23.550
I'll see...

22
00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:27.440
Jerk. I was talking...

23
00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:29.350
Mr. Cho's almost here.

24
00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.310
Get out!

25
00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:17.390
Get out now!

26
00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.840
Shoot!

27
00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:49.220
Damn it...

28
00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:11.720
It's been a while. friend.

29
00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:17.570
I told you
you would see me again soon.

30
00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:19.940
You... wait...

31
00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:22.870
It's just...

32
00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:26.290
Oh yeah. I said
I would give you money.

33
00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:28.920
I'll give it to you for real!

34
00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.680
I'm not lying this time.
you'll get it. okay?

35
00:04:37.409 --> 00:04:38.470
It's fine.

36
00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:41.159
Friends shouldn't pay
each other money.

37
00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:00.110
Don't kill me!
Please don't kill me!

38
00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:01.800
Goddammit. what are you doing?!

39
00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:02.720
You got blood on my shoe!

40
00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:03.800
Idiot!

41
00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:10.590
Jackass. it's this season's
brand-new model!

42
00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:12.590
I barely managed to buy it
from the first batch!

43
00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:16.400
I could just kill you!

44
00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:37.650
Look at it.

45
00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:41.620
I'm going to use this

46
00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:44.590
to carve your heart out.

47
00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:46.840
You know what?

48
00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:49.250
Blunt instruments are more painful

49
00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:52.540
than sharp knives.

50
00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.500
You can't die quick with these.

51
00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:56.800
How much is your client
paying you?

52
00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:58.830
I'll pay you double...

53
00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:07.580
Friend. you said we're friends!

54
00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:08.990
Don't kill me. please!

55
00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:10.070
Right. friend.

56
00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:12.210
I told you.

57
00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:18.680
I'm the last friend you'll meet

58
00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:20.880
before you die.

59
00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:23.780
It's nothing personal.

60
00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:26.190
We're pros.
and this is just business.

61
00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:44.020
(The Childe)

62
00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:05.520
Nice work today Marco.

63
00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:25.610
You promised me more
from this match onwards.

64
00:08:31.850 --> 00:08:32.850
Hey Marco!

65
00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:34.260
You eat well

66
00:08:34.289 --> 00:08:35.929
and take care of
yourself with that money!

67
00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:38.130
You know about the big match
next week. right?

68
00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:40.080
I put a load of money on you!

69
00:08:41.039 --> 00:08:42.140
Arrogant jerk...

70
00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:43.950
Damn Kopino half-breed...!

71
00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:18.990
Got your butt kicked this time?

72
00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.790
Your opponent was a Thai?

73
00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:31.760
Those Thais sure got
spicy punches.

74
00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:34.530
Someone really did a number

75
00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:36.460
on our mighty Marco's face.

76
00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:41.120
Don't glare at me. idiot.

77
00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:43.440
How's your mother?

78
00:10:47.690 --> 00:10:50.030
She should really get
that surgery soon.

79
00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:52.490
What brings you here today?

80
00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:54.610
Because of your father?

81
00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:58.190
Any news?

82
00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:03.730
Nothing so far.

83
00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:06.940
But hang in there.

84
00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:10.000
If he's alive.
you might find him one day.

85
00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:12.740
I wouldn't even be
looking for that man

86
00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:14.820
if it wasn't for Mom's operation.

87
00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:17.490
Come on now.

88
00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:22.200
What's that?

89
00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:26.480
Use it to hire someone in Korea
to look for him.

90
00:11:27.340 --> 00:11:29.300
Hey! Hey!

91
00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:32.330
Marco!
Marco!

92
00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:51.600
You're later than usual.

93
00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:54.400
LaLiga's it's closed already

94
00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:57.580
but Premier League
is still betting.

95
00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:00.300
Which team has the highest odds?

96
00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:03.310
Let's see...

97
00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:06.550
Um. Burnley?

98
00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:08.770
Yeah. it's Burnley.

99
00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:10.220
They're going against Chelsea.

100
00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:11.890
What are the odds?

101
00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:14.420
250 to 1.

102
00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:17.750
All on Burnley.

103
00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:21.540
Hey Marco.
that's not a great idea.

104
00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:23.520
Why don't you just buy
the lotto ticket?

105
00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:25.170
You'll have a better
chance of winning.

106
00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:27.630
I said all on Burnley.

107
00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:30.320
Ay Gago.

108
00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:42.930
It's on me. mate.

109
00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:45.250
Long time no see Marco.

110
00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:48.500
That last fight was sick. Huh?

111
00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:51.250
Big shot Thai guy
didn't stand a chance.

112
00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:54.290
Thanks to you
I made a pretty penny.

113
00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:55.920
Um? Thanks for that.

114
00:12:57.290 --> 00:12:58.320
Oh yeah. So ah...

115
00:12:59.150 --> 00:13:00.540
how's searching for daddy going?

116
00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:01.620
Any leads?

117
00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:08.140
- Of course not...
- Why do you care?

118
00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:13.740
But I do have a job
that might interest you.

119
00:13:15.530 --> 00:13:18.800
I've had my eye on this
fancy jewelry store downtown.

120
00:13:19.220 --> 00:13:22.350
I'm going to get to work on it...
You want in?

121
00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:25.070
Come on. man.

122
00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:27.450
All you have to do is
cut the power

123
00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:28.690
and keep the security busy.

124
00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:31.090
You don't even have to go in
and I'll give you 10%.

125
00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:33.170
Store that size...

126
00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:34.590
even with the middleman.

127
00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:36.460
it'll be 100 big ones. easy.

128
00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:40.180
10%. Marco.

129
00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:41.660
What do you say?

130
00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:45.690
- I'll think about it.
- Come on. man!

131
00:13:45.770 --> 00:13:46.890
What's there to think about?

132
00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:48.650
You know what.

133
00:13:49.420 --> 00:13:51.890
I'll even forget
about mommy's medication.

134
00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.820
(Chelsea 4:0)

135
00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:38.450
(Yo. Chelsea took all your money.)

136
00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:48.860
When you go around the back
to the building

137
00:14:48.940 --> 00:14:51.920
you'll find the power box
and a guard booth.

138
00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:54.070
Here.

139
00:14:57.010 --> 00:14:58.460
They'll bust in as soon as you

140
00:14:58.540 --> 00:14:59.390
keep the guards to busy

141
00:14:59.470 --> 00:15:00.670
cut the power to the building.

142
00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:02.320
No problem.

143
00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:25.200
Get back jerks!

144
00:17:06.930 --> 00:17:08.849
Hey! Are you okay?

145
00:17:11.470 --> 00:17:12.740
Oh no. are you okay?

146
00:17:12.819 --> 00:17:15.310
I didn't see you run out...

147
00:17:17.099 --> 00:17:19.369
We should go to the hospital...

148
00:17:20.020 --> 00:17:21.810
Why am I speaking Korean?

149
00:17:22.990 --> 00:17:24.130
I'm really sorry.

150
00:17:24.210 --> 00:17:25.970
We should go to
the hospital right away.

151
00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:28.500
Korean?

152
00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:31.760
- Are you Korean?
- What?

153
00:17:34.220 --> 00:17:36.140
Well. not exactly.

154
00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:20.460
How are you feeling?

155
00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:23.260
All the tests came back well.

156
00:18:23.340 --> 00:18:25.570
I told you this was unnecessary.

157
00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:26.776
we could've settled last night.

158
00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:28.030
what was the point of this?

159
00:18:28.110 --> 00:18:29.110
Even so.

160
00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:31.330
you just never know
about accidents.

161
00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:33.260
There could be lasting effects.

162
00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:38.050
This isn't much. please take it.

163
00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:39.600
and I'm so sorry.

164
00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:47.710
By the way. you speak
Korean really well.

165
00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:49.220
You look like one too.

166
00:18:49.300 --> 00:18:51.570
anyone will think
that you're a Korean.

167
00:18:52.780 --> 00:18:54.180
I get that a lot.

168
00:18:54.260 --> 00:18:56.690
Did you learn Korean somewhere?

169
00:18:59.210 --> 00:19:00.640
Or are you...

170
00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:03.410
what was it called? Kopino?

171
00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:05.710
You are. right?

172
00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:12.050
Sorry. I shouldn't have
said that...

173
00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:37.650
Yeah?

174
00:19:40.850 --> 00:19:41.850
What?

175
00:19:53.260 --> 00:19:56.290
I was going to take your money.

176
00:19:56.370 --> 00:19:58.610
but it stank
so badly of your sweat.

177
00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:05.700
It would be proper to say
that they found us.

178
00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:08.590
rather than us looking for them.

179
00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:13.950
It means your father
did not forget about you.

180
00:20:14.030 --> 00:20:17.220
As you know.
cases like this are so rare.

181
00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:18.660
How many fathers

182
00:20:18.740 --> 00:20:21.920
came looking for
their Kopino kids here?

183
00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:23.490
None. zero.

184
00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:27.530
They just plant their seeds and
get the hell out of here.

185
00:20:28.530 --> 00:20:30.050
When is he coming?

186
00:20:30.130 --> 00:20:32.510
Oh yeah. he's coming right away.

187
00:20:32.590 --> 00:20:34.190
It looked like he was in a hurry.

188
00:20:35.950 --> 00:20:38.690
And this is my gift to you.

189
00:20:38.770 --> 00:20:40.260
It's a Korean calling card.

190
00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:44.020
You might need it there.
so keep it with you.

191
00:21:12.590 --> 00:21:13.970
What a stench.

192
00:21:53.930 --> 00:21:54.930
Marco Han?

193
00:21:57.970 --> 00:21:59.120
You're him.

194
00:22:00.850 --> 00:22:01.850
Good to meet you.

195
00:22:16.590 --> 00:22:17.900
Thank you.

196
00:22:32.560 --> 00:22:33.816
(Law Firm The Royal Partner
Kang Won-seok)

197
00:22:33.840 --> 00:22:36.570
Your father's a bit sick.

198
00:22:36.650 --> 00:22:38.540
so I came instead.

199
00:22:39.440 --> 00:22:41.780
Do you understand
what I just said?

200
00:22:42.860 --> 00:22:45.980
I don't speak Tagalog at all.

201
00:22:46.060 --> 00:22:47.780
but a little English.
would you prefer that?

202
00:22:49.840 --> 00:22:51.820
It's okay. you can speak Korean.

203
00:22:53.740 --> 00:22:56.000
You speak Korean so well.

204
00:22:56.080 --> 00:22:58.800
Mom forced me to
speak Korean or English.

205
00:22:59.540 --> 00:23:00.900
I had to go to a Korean school.

206
00:23:00.980 --> 00:23:02.350
Korean school?

207
00:23:21.140 --> 00:23:23.500
You need those to fly.

208
00:23:24.170 --> 00:23:26.220
Passport. visa and such.

209
00:23:27.310 --> 00:23:29.250
Isn't money great?

210
00:23:29.330 --> 00:23:30.800
Anything is solvable with it.

211
00:23:34.030 --> 00:23:35.870
Han. look here.

212
00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:38.750
She's a hospice
who will look after your mother.

213
00:23:38.830 --> 00:23:40.270
Because of your father's
condition.

214
00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:42.040
we have to hurry.

215
00:23:42.120 --> 00:23:44.400
Pack lightly and come out.

216
00:23:46.540 --> 00:23:47.870
Right now?

217
00:23:47.950 --> 00:23:49.740
Why? Is there a problem?

218
00:23:50.420 --> 00:23:51.420
But...

219
00:23:56.020 --> 00:24:00.060
For her sake. wouldn't it be best
to head out as soon as possible?

220
00:24:00.140 --> 00:24:01.230
Paying for her surgery is

221
00:24:01.310 --> 00:24:04.670
not even a bother to him.

222
00:24:04.750 --> 00:24:06.740
He'll probably take care of it
right away.

223
00:24:08.080 --> 00:24:10.050
It's a quick flight to Seoul.

224
00:24:10.130 --> 00:24:12.480
Pack up quickly. okay?

225
00:24:12.560 --> 00:24:14.380
He really wants to see you.

226
00:24:26.440 --> 00:24:28.200
(Hokyung Foundation
Accused of Slush Fund...)

227
00:24:28.970 --> 00:24:31.620
(Illegal Succession
at Hokyung Foundation...)

228
00:24:31.700 --> 00:24:34.060
(Hokyung Foundation's Slush Fund.
Whistleblowers Missing...)

229
00:24:43.540 --> 00:24:45.950
(Attorney Kang Won-seok)

230
00:24:49.600 --> 00:24:50.950
(Attorney Kang Won-seok)

231
00:25:01.420 --> 00:25:04.300
Yes. Kang. how did it go?

232
00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:09.070
Very good. that's great.

233
00:25:11.760 --> 00:25:12.850
When's the flight?

234
00:25:16.720 --> 00:25:17.740
Okay.

235
00:25:19.340 --> 00:25:23.570
I'll have everyone on standby.
come here at once.

236
00:25:25.680 --> 00:25:27.530
Okay. good.

237
00:25:34.730 --> 00:25:36.190
So? how did it go?

238
00:25:36.270 --> 00:25:37.270
Sir?

239
00:25:38.290 --> 00:25:42.590
Thankfully. their editors
are quite amicable to us.

240
00:25:42.670 --> 00:25:44.130
so we managed to
kill all articles.

241
00:25:44.210 --> 00:25:45.120
Return for what?

242
00:25:45.200 --> 00:25:49.180
We will be the main sponsor
for Daeil Daily's annual

243
00:25:49.260 --> 00:25:51.840
corporation expo
for the next 3 years.

244
00:25:51.920 --> 00:25:52.920
For the other 3 outlets.

245
00:25:53.000 --> 00:25:54.036
we'll be the main ad client...

246
00:25:54.060 --> 00:25:55.570
So pathetic...

247
00:25:58.030 --> 00:26:01.170
It's so easy taking
someone else's money.

248
00:26:01.810 --> 00:26:03.150
It's a sensitive period.

249
00:26:03.530 --> 00:26:07.500
it'd be best not to get mixed up
with malicious tabloids.

250
00:26:08.210 --> 00:26:09.230
I know.

251
00:26:10.670 --> 00:26:13.440
Do I look like an idiot
who can't read the room?

252
00:26:13.520 --> 00:26:15.390
That's not what I meant.

253
00:26:15.470 --> 00:26:18.110
- Whatever.
- Sir?

254
00:26:18.190 --> 00:26:20.810
- That'll be all.
- Yes. sir.

255
00:26:24.910 --> 00:26:27.170
You haven't been here
in a long time.

256
00:26:27.250 --> 00:26:29.760
Get some rest
and see you tomorrow.

257
00:26:29.840 --> 00:26:33.290
That's all right. sir.
I'll head back to Seoul...

258
00:26:34.990 --> 00:26:36.510
As you wish. sir.

259
00:26:36.590 --> 00:26:38.670
There's someone
I want you to meet.

260
00:26:39.630 --> 00:26:40.960
so let's have breakfast tomorrow.

261
00:26:41.040 --> 00:26:42.160
Yes. sir.

262
00:26:43.980 --> 00:26:44.980
This way.

263
00:27:02.380 --> 00:27:06.260
So. father.
how are you holding up?

264
00:27:10.920 --> 00:27:12.610
They're leaving the Philippines.

265
00:27:12.690 --> 00:27:13.690
so just hang in there.

266
00:27:17.330 --> 00:27:18.350
What did you say?

267
00:27:21.550 --> 00:27:24.750
Yes. father. the youngest.

268
00:27:25.390 --> 00:27:28.820
That youngest son you've been
waiting for is on the way.

269
00:27:29.810 --> 00:27:30.860
Happy?

270
00:27:33.940 --> 00:27:34.940
Are you?

271
00:27:38.770 --> 00:27:41.870
Yes. that mutt.

272
00:27:47.180 --> 00:27:49.200
Your mutt's on the way here.

273
00:27:50.540 --> 00:27:54.350
Just hang on
until he arrives. okay?

274
00:28:01.740 --> 00:28:03.070
We don't have time.

275
00:28:03.150 --> 00:28:06.110
Have the cars on standby
so that we can leave immediately.

276
00:28:06.190 --> 00:28:07.310
Understood. sir.

277
00:29:15.280 --> 00:29:17.800
Man. I almost missed it.

278
00:29:17.880 --> 00:29:20.060
I thought you'd leave tomorrow.

279
00:29:20.140 --> 00:29:21.590
but returning on the same day?

280
00:29:22.250 --> 00:29:24.070
They must really be in a hurry.

281
00:29:25.460 --> 00:29:28.150
They're filthy rich.
putting you in business class?

282
00:29:32.560 --> 00:29:34.190
Who am I?

283
00:29:35.730 --> 00:29:36.780
A friend.

284
00:29:38.510 --> 00:29:40.750
Consider me a friend for now.

285
00:29:41.390 --> 00:29:42.940
Listen. friend.

286
00:29:43.020 --> 00:29:44.940
You're heading to Korea.

287
00:29:46.420 --> 00:29:48.870
do you even know why you're going?

288
00:29:50.670 --> 00:29:51.670
What?

289
00:29:52.210 --> 00:29:53.550
There's no way you would.

290
00:29:57.580 --> 00:29:59.256
Oh yeah. isn't this
your first time in Korea?

291
00:29:59.280 --> 00:30:00.750
Should I give you a tip?

292
00:30:04.340 --> 00:30:05.910
This will help you out big time.

293
00:30:06.450 --> 00:30:07.990
Once you're there.

294
00:30:08.070 --> 00:30:10.050
use English whenever possible.

295
00:30:10.130 --> 00:30:12.840
Koreans love
English speaking people.

296
00:30:12.920 --> 00:30:14.970
Hey. this works. For sure.

297
00:30:15.050 --> 00:30:16.340
One hundred percent.

298
00:30:17.040 --> 00:30:19.670
And of course.
an American accent is the best.

299
00:30:19.980 --> 00:30:23.380
Pretend like a 2nd.
or 3rd generation Korean-American.

300
00:30:24.920 --> 00:30:25.800
Trust me.

301
00:30:25.880 --> 00:30:27.730
They'll do whatever...

302
00:30:29.710 --> 00:30:32.800
A British accent is okay too.

303
00:30:32.880 --> 00:30:35.820
but Koreans aren't
really used to it.

304
00:30:36.140 --> 00:30:40.130
So an American accent is the best.

305
00:30:40.210 --> 00:30:41.870
works everytime.

306
00:30:42.280 --> 00:30:43.160
Hey…

307
00:30:43.240 --> 00:30:44.756
But don't use
a Southeast Asian accent.

308
00:30:44.780 --> 00:30:46.590
Never. ever!

309
00:30:46.670 --> 00:30:48.450
Better off not using it.

310
00:30:48.530 --> 00:30:50.220
You have to be careful.

311
00:30:54.380 --> 00:30:56.140
No point in tipping off
that you're a Kopino.

312
00:30:58.860 --> 00:31:01.040
- Am I right?
- Who are you?

313
00:31:02.130 --> 00:31:04.400
Like I said. an amigo. a friend.

314
00:31:05.810 --> 00:31:09.870
I may be
the last friend in your life.

315
00:31:10.730 --> 00:31:12.780
- What?
- By the way...

316
00:31:13.260 --> 00:31:16.100
if we go by age.
I'm actually older.

317
00:31:16.180 --> 00:31:19.150
I look young
but I got a few years on you.

318
00:31:20.140 --> 00:31:22.040
So. you shouldn't swear

319
00:31:22.120 --> 00:31:23.780
just because we're friends.

320
00:31:23.860 --> 00:31:25.600
I really hate rude jerks.

321
00:31:25.680 --> 00:31:27.380
What are you on about?

322
00:31:27.890 --> 00:31:29.410
Who said I was going to
be your friend?

323
00:31:29.450 --> 00:31:32.560
Life never works out
the way you intended. bud.

324
00:31:33.230 --> 00:31:36.020
Your English pronunciation
is quite good.

325
00:31:36.500 --> 00:31:38.050
What are you talking about!

326
00:31:38.130 --> 00:31:39.010
Excuse me.

327
00:31:39.090 --> 00:31:41.790
May I ask you
to return to your seat?

328
00:31:41.870 --> 00:31:43.760
- Of course.
- Thank you.

329
00:31:54.990 --> 00:31:57.180
Think about it.

330
00:31:57.260 --> 00:31:58.610
Isn't it fishy?

331
00:31:59.210 --> 00:32:01.760
Going to another country
on a plane

332
00:32:01.840 --> 00:32:04.490
isn't like walking to a local bar.

333
00:32:05.200 --> 00:32:07.140
It's not that simple.

334
00:32:07.220 --> 00:32:09.140
Visa. passport. and all that.

335
00:32:11.340 --> 00:32:14.000
It's weird. don't you think?

336
00:32:18.830 --> 00:32:20.810
Should I tell you
why you're going to Korea?

337
00:32:31.090 --> 00:32:32.090
I'm off.

338
00:32:33.390 --> 00:32:34.480
See you soon.

339
00:32:38.670 --> 00:32:39.730
Crazy ass...!

340
00:33:02.510 --> 00:33:05.600
Yeah. we just touched down.

341
00:33:05.680 --> 00:33:07.660
No. I'm on a delivery run.

342
00:33:08.910 --> 00:33:10.290
Where are you?

343
00:33:10.860 --> 00:33:13.390
Me? I'm in a business meeting.

344
00:33:16.720 --> 00:33:17.810
Yeah.

345
00:33:20.180 --> 00:33:21.180
Yeah.

346
00:33:28.880 --> 00:33:32.610
How did you return so quickly
after the clean up?

347
00:33:32.690 --> 00:33:35.060
Don't worry.
I did everything as per my order.

348
00:33:36.620 --> 00:33:38.850
I cleaned it up nicely.

349
00:33:38.930 --> 00:33:40.530
We were never there.

350
00:33:42.640 --> 00:33:44.860
So my job's finished?

351
00:33:44.940 --> 00:33:46.860
There's no end to our work.

352
00:33:49.230 --> 00:33:51.360
- Is he the one?
- Yeah.

353
00:33:51.440 --> 00:33:52.750
Put him inside.

354
00:34:23.820 --> 00:34:26.270
Damn. my brother's hot.

355
00:34:26.350 --> 00:34:29.659
Doesn't he look like a celebrity?
Take a look.

356
00:34:29.739 --> 00:34:30.929
So similar. right?

357
00:34:31.659 --> 00:34:32.659
Who?

358
00:34:35.540 --> 00:34:38.239
Right. you don't watch TV.

359
00:34:38.320 --> 00:34:40.820
Too bad. that guy's hot too.

360
00:34:42.670 --> 00:34:46.020
Look at his muscles.
those are so dope.

361
00:34:46.100 --> 00:34:48.159
Real dope.
Yeah?

362
00:34:48.239 --> 00:34:50.770
So? What will you do?

363
00:34:51.310 --> 00:34:52.310
Do what?

364
00:34:55.600 --> 00:34:58.030
Just stick to the original order.

365
00:34:59.060 --> 00:35:00.060
Okay.

366
00:35:01.610 --> 00:35:02.800
By the way...

367
00:35:05.550 --> 00:35:07.220
what about the favor I asked you?

368
00:35:11.540 --> 00:35:12.910
I brought it.

369
00:35:14.640 --> 00:35:16.060
but do you really need it?

370
00:35:16.140 --> 00:35:19.280
You never know.
I'm preparing for the worst.

371
00:35:19.980 --> 00:35:20.980
Better safe than sorry.

372
00:35:21.040 --> 00:35:22.650
Don't worry. I practiced a lot.

373
00:35:22.730 --> 00:35:24.770
Damn it.
I'm going to be late for school.

374
00:35:24.850 --> 00:35:25.950
Yoon-ju. I have to go.

375
00:35:26.030 --> 00:35:28.400
Thank you!
See you later!

376
00:36:33.010 --> 00:36:36.850
It sure is stunning here.

377
00:36:38.260 --> 00:36:40.430
Great water. great air...

378
00:37:17.010 --> 00:37:20.990
Director Han. sir.
why are you doing this to me?

379
00:37:21.070 --> 00:37:23.040
Director Han! What's going on?!

380
00:37:23.120 --> 00:37:26.560
You are making a huge mistake!

381
00:37:26.640 --> 00:37:28.610
You know who I am!

382
00:37:28.690 --> 00:37:30.540
How will you handle
the backlash...

383
00:37:34.800 --> 00:37:36.550
That's enough.

384
00:37:37.300 --> 00:37:40.940
Please keep your mouths shut.
your breath stinks.

385
00:37:43.630 --> 00:37:46.800
So. are you two well acquainted?

386
00:37:48.500 --> 00:37:51.020
No need to play dumb.

387
00:38:07.380 --> 00:38:10.670
You're not just well acquainted.

388
00:38:11.660 --> 00:38:14.140
you gentlemen are
practically best friends.

389
00:38:14.220 --> 00:38:17.390
Even so. this is plain nasty.

390
00:38:18.290 --> 00:38:21.200
You hold great authority
and honor in this society.

391
00:38:22.580 --> 00:38:25.390
Am I right. Mr. Publisher?

392
00:38:29.900 --> 00:38:31.096
(Hokyung Foundation
Accused of Slush Fund...)

393
00:38:31.120 --> 00:38:32.566
Illegal Succession
at Hokyung Foundation...

394
00:38:32.590 --> 00:38:34.210
You have no problem
sucking others dry.

395
00:38:34.290 --> 00:38:35.840
what are you?

396
00:38:35.920 --> 00:38:37.550
A tick or a parasite?

397
00:38:38.540 --> 00:38:42.540
This guy fed you this. right?

398
00:38:42.990 --> 00:38:44.690
(Hokyung in Hot Waters
Over Slush Fund...)

399
00:38:45.780 --> 00:38:46.710
I'm an impatient type.

400
00:38:46.790 --> 00:38:48.880
could you answer right away?

401
00:38:49.520 --> 00:38:50.640
Yes. yes!

402
00:38:59.310 --> 00:39:01.760
How many years have you
worked with my father?

403
00:39:01.840 --> 00:39:04.590
19 years? 20?

404
00:39:05.810 --> 00:39:10.610
This is why I have
trust issues with humans.

405
00:39:14.700 --> 00:39:16.280
You've swapped allegiance to Jang

406
00:39:16.360 --> 00:39:17.396
after backstabbing my father?

407
00:39:17.420 --> 00:39:20.860
Director Han. that's not it.
please listen to me.

408
00:39:20.940 --> 00:39:21.950
Please. just this once.

409
00:39:22.030 --> 00:39:24.100
I have to tell you something...

410
00:39:24.180 --> 00:39:25.650
You think Jang will win?

411
00:39:27.340 --> 00:39:29.280
Isn't that why you did this?

412
00:39:29.360 --> 00:39:31.740
Director Han. please hear me out!

413
00:39:31.820 --> 00:39:35.250
Please listen to me.
I got something to tell you...

414
00:39:36.210 --> 00:39:38.530
You were here
when this was built. weren't you?

415
00:39:38.610 --> 00:39:40.750
This is about
2.8 million square feet. right?

416
00:39:41.940 --> 00:39:44.530
Cedar forest over there.

417
00:39:45.200 --> 00:39:48.700
and there. what's that tree?

418
00:39:48.780 --> 00:39:52.700
- Cypress tree. sir.
- Right. cypress tree.

419
00:39:52.780 --> 00:39:55.070
And even more forests beyond that.

420
00:39:55.920 --> 00:39:58.670
There's not a single soul
within a 10 km radius.

421
00:40:00.500 --> 00:40:01.970
Aren't you curious?

422
00:40:04.430 --> 00:40:07.920
These missing people.
where could they have gone?

423
00:40:08.600 --> 00:40:09.470
(Hokyung Foundation's Slush Fund.
Whistleblowers Missing...)

424
00:40:09.550 --> 00:40:10.930
Isn't that why you wrote it?

425
00:40:16.820 --> 00:40:18.000
They're all here.

426
00:40:35.300 --> 00:40:38.580
Director Han.
please don't kill me!

427
00:40:38.660 --> 00:40:39.830
Please. don't kill me!

428
00:40:42.370 --> 00:40:43.470
What? What?

429
00:40:43.550 --> 00:40:45.430
Sensitive period. right?

430
00:40:46.970 --> 00:40:49.260
Don't worry about your family.

431
00:40:49.340 --> 00:40:52.850
I sent all those photos
to your families.

432
00:40:52.930 --> 00:40:54.420
Every single one.

433
00:40:54.500 --> 00:40:57.230
Not just to your wives.
but to all your children too.

434
00:40:57.310 --> 00:40:59.910
So. don't you worry.

435
00:41:00.510 --> 00:41:01.960
That's not all.

436
00:41:02.040 --> 00:41:04.220
those are plastered
all over the internet.

437
00:41:05.820 --> 00:41:09.270
So both of you have disappeared.

438
00:41:09.350 --> 00:41:11.150
leaving behind a will.

439
00:41:11.230 --> 00:41:12.660
No one will find you. right?

440
00:41:12.740 --> 00:41:14.060
Why would anyone look for you.

441
00:41:14.140 --> 00:41:15.740
after seeing these?

442
00:41:21.530 --> 00:41:23.260
Untie him. right now!

443
00:41:33.380 --> 00:41:38.180
Director Han. I'll do my best!

444
00:41:39.330 --> 00:41:41.540
Sir. please!

445
00:41:44.450 --> 00:41:46.050
Look at you.

446
00:41:49.150 --> 00:41:50.180
For old times sake.

447
00:41:50.260 --> 00:41:51.840
I'll give you a chance.

448
00:41:53.410 --> 00:41:56.080
See that forest over there?

449
00:41:56.160 --> 00:41:58.290
The cedar forest.

450
00:41:58.370 --> 00:41:59.860
If you reach there.

451
00:41:59.940 --> 00:42:01.280
I'll let you live.

452
00:42:03.040 --> 00:42:06.370
Good? Let's run. are you ready?

453
00:42:09.280 --> 00:42:10.590
One second! Hold on!

454
00:42:12.860 --> 00:42:14.770
Run in a zigzag.

455
00:42:14.850 --> 00:42:17.580
You'll have a lower chance
of getting shot.

456
00:42:17.660 --> 00:42:20.220
- Thank you.
- What are you doing. get ready.

457
00:42:22.010 --> 00:42:26.380
Start running on three.

458
00:42:26.460 --> 00:42:28.250
I'll start shooting after 10.

459
00:42:29.730 --> 00:42:30.730
Here we go.

460
00:42:31.860 --> 00:42:32.860
One.

461
00:42:34.920 --> 00:42:35.920
Two.

462
00:42:47.620 --> 00:42:50.350
I said to run on three.

463
00:42:50.430 --> 00:42:52.670
he couldn't listen
to save himself.

464
00:43:08.200 --> 00:43:09.880
Dr. Lee. have you slept well?

465
00:43:09.960 --> 00:43:11.280
Yes. thanks to you.

466
00:43:11.360 --> 00:43:13.830
- Have you heard?
- Yes.

467
00:43:14.440 --> 00:43:16.520
Everything is perfect. isn't it?

468
00:43:17.220 --> 00:43:19.910
Please don't disappoint me
this time.

469
00:43:22.470 --> 00:43:26.240
It's almost time.
please go prepare.

470
00:43:48.200 --> 00:43:50.920
Kid. how old are you?

471
00:43:54.340 --> 00:43:57.030
Punk. I just asked you a question.

472
00:43:58.310 --> 00:43:59.970
How old are you. jerk?

473
00:44:01.220 --> 00:44:02.340
Twenty-four.

474
00:44:04.290 --> 00:44:05.150
Speak Korean.

475
00:44:05.230 --> 00:44:06.160
I know you speak it.

476
00:44:06.240 --> 00:44:08.030
What an idiot.

477
00:44:08.710 --> 00:44:10.260
You don't even
understand the basics?

478
00:44:10.340 --> 00:44:12.000
He said 24.

479
00:44:13.160 --> 00:44:14.400
Oh. 24.

480
00:44:15.010 --> 00:44:16.500
Learn basic English. will you?

481
00:44:16.580 --> 00:44:18.400
Learning it won't kill you.

482
00:44:18.980 --> 00:44:19.980
Sure.

483
00:44:23.300 --> 00:44:24.920
So full of vitality.

484
00:44:25.000 --> 00:44:26.740
a long way
from the expiration date.

485
00:44:26.820 --> 00:44:29.970
Shut your damn mouth
and stick to driving!

486
00:44:30.050 --> 00:44:31.050
Yes. sir.

487
00:44:41.700 --> 00:44:42.700
What's that?

488
00:45:03.620 --> 00:45:05.290
Why isn't he overtaking me

489
00:45:05.370 --> 00:45:06.690
if he's so damn busy?

490
00:45:08.290 --> 00:45:09.600
What the heck?

491
00:45:15.280 --> 00:45:16.720
Increase speed.

492
00:45:16.800 --> 00:45:18.440
What the hell for?

493
00:45:20.160 --> 00:45:21.920
Buddy! Hey!

494
00:45:22.470 --> 00:45:23.940
You sure drive like an idiot!

495
00:45:24.020 --> 00:45:26.760
- Step on it! Now!
- Stop the car!

496
00:46:04.920 --> 00:46:06.350
(Unknown Caller ID)

497
00:46:07.030 --> 00:46:08.080
Who is this?

498
00:46:10.610 --> 00:46:11.610
What?

499
00:46:15.570 --> 00:46:16.570
So?

500
00:46:19.560 --> 00:46:21.090
Who are you guys?

501
00:46:34.340 --> 00:46:35.340
What?

502
00:46:38.180 --> 00:46:39.200
How much?

503
00:46:51.680 --> 00:46:52.680
Hey.

504
00:46:54.210 --> 00:46:55.970
Get everyone on standby.

505
00:47:15.680 --> 00:47:16.960
Marco!

506
00:48:03.040 --> 00:48:04.960
Mercedes really is the bomb.

507
00:48:05.920 --> 00:48:07.550
It's worth every penny.

508
00:48:08.420 --> 00:48:11.580
Hey friend. good to see you.

509
00:48:13.370 --> 00:48:14.780
I told you we'd see
each other soon.

510
00:48:18.300 --> 00:48:22.620
There's a reason
why people go nuts over Mercedes.

511
00:48:23.450 --> 00:48:24.466
If you get into an accident
like that

512
00:48:24.490 --> 00:48:25.650
without seatbelts.

513
00:48:25.730 --> 00:48:27.520
everyone should be dead.

514
00:48:28.610 --> 00:48:29.630
Am I right?

515
00:48:33.220 --> 00:48:35.900
Friend. are you scared?

516
00:48:37.570 --> 00:48:39.680
There's no need to be.
relax. ease up.

517
00:48:46.180 --> 00:48:47.370
What are you looking at?

518
00:48:47.450 --> 00:48:48.960
Thinking of taking off?

519
00:48:52.900 --> 00:48:54.340
That won't be easy.

520
00:48:55.900 --> 00:48:57.220
Who are you?

521
00:48:59.040 --> 00:49:00.240
Tell me.

522
00:49:00.320 --> 00:49:02.220
I told you. a friend.

523
00:49:02.300 --> 00:49:04.560
- A friend?
- Yes. that's right.

524
00:49:04.640 --> 00:49:06.850
And this is...

525
00:49:06.930 --> 00:49:08.350
my job.

526
00:49:09.020 --> 00:49:10.800
Why are you doing this to me?

527
00:49:10.880 --> 00:49:12.930
It's a bit tough

528
00:49:13.320 --> 00:49:17.340
to explain everything
to you right now.

529
00:49:18.430 --> 00:49:20.570
But don't worry.

530
00:49:22.010 --> 00:49:24.330
You'll find out for yourself

531
00:49:24.410 --> 00:49:26.130
when it's time for you to die.

532
00:49:26.210 --> 00:49:27.090
What?

533
00:49:27.170 --> 00:49:29.060
I told you in the airplane.

534
00:49:31.170 --> 00:49:32.420
that you came here to die.

535
00:49:32.500 --> 00:49:33.700
You're going there to die.

536
00:49:40.030 --> 00:49:41.740
Stop talking nonsense. prick.

537
00:49:41.820 --> 00:49:43.680
Prick... What?

538
00:49:44.190 --> 00:49:46.010
Buddy! Where are you going?

539
00:49:52.480 --> 00:49:54.020
He speaks Korean so well.

540
00:51:08.030 --> 00:51:09.600
Hey! Buddy!

541
00:51:10.590 --> 00:51:11.810
Stop! Hey!

542
00:51:36.260 --> 00:51:38.450
It's a lot higher than I thought.

543
00:51:38.530 --> 00:51:40.510
You okay?

544
00:51:41.210 --> 00:51:44.670
Jerk. you got a death wish?

545
00:51:46.080 --> 00:51:47.520
You prick!

546
00:51:48.480 --> 00:51:49.970
Get over here. you prick!

547
00:51:50.050 --> 00:51:51.260
Shut your mouth.

548
00:52:54.050 --> 00:52:55.070
Lord...

549
00:53:00.540 --> 00:53:01.540
Dammit!

550
00:53:51.650 --> 00:53:55.420
Huh? Very nice. that's great.

551
00:54:15.940 --> 00:54:17.790
Director. we found it.

552
00:54:28.420 --> 00:54:29.760
Professional?

553
00:54:32.480 --> 00:54:34.340
These idiots...

554
00:54:40.900 --> 00:54:45.410
Father. looks like
we got a proper roadblock.

555
00:54:48.260 --> 00:54:50.050
We got some hyenas around.

556
00:54:50.810 --> 00:54:52.130
I don't know who these guys are.

557
00:54:52.210 --> 00:54:54.560
but they're going all out.

558
00:54:57.120 --> 00:54:58.250
Since you're down.

559
00:54:58.330 --> 00:55:00.430
they think we're weak.

560
00:55:00.510 --> 00:55:04.030
and ambushing us. these jerks.

561
00:55:08.380 --> 00:55:10.530
He wants $10 million.

562
00:55:11.260 --> 00:55:14.110
He wants $10 million
for that mutt.

563
00:55:21.500 --> 00:55:24.290
It's all ready. sir.

564
00:55:26.620 --> 00:55:27.620
Okay.

565
00:55:35.390 --> 00:55:36.830
Just hang in there.

566
00:55:38.460 --> 00:55:41.210
I'll go get that mutt myself.

567
00:56:22.690 --> 00:56:24.640
(Law Firm The Royal Partner
Kang Won-seok)

568
00:56:28.160 --> 00:56:33.760
(Law Firm The Royal Partner
Kang Won-seok)

569
00:56:36.220 --> 00:56:38.990
Hello. this is Law Firm The Royal.

570
00:56:39.070 --> 00:56:41.840
Please stay on the line.
we'll connect you right away.

571
00:56:41.920 --> 00:56:46.300
(Call Forwarding)

572
00:56:48.830 --> 00:56:50.690
- Hello?
- Hello?

573
00:56:52.610 --> 00:56:55.650
Seriously?
That could've been terrible.

574
00:56:56.700 --> 00:56:58.800
Where are you now?

575
00:56:58.880 --> 00:57:00.750
Yes. I know where that is.

576
00:57:00.830 --> 00:57:02.810
I'm on my way.
so stay right there.

577
00:57:28.580 --> 00:57:30.320
Mr. Kim. it's Marco!

578
00:57:30.400 --> 00:57:31.400
Where are you?

579
00:57:31.430 --> 00:57:33.260
I'm getting calls
saying you disappeared!

580
00:57:33.340 --> 00:57:35.680
Someone's trying to kill me.

581
00:57:36.130 --> 00:57:37.620
Everyone I came with are all dead!

582
00:57:37.700 --> 00:57:40.030
What the heck are you saying?

583
00:57:40.640 --> 00:57:41.980
Have you contacted your father?

584
00:57:43.420 --> 00:57:44.420
You punk.

585
00:58:14.880 --> 00:58:16.380
Idiot.

586
00:58:24.640 --> 00:58:25.790
Hey. friend!

587
00:58:26.980 --> 00:58:30.500
Didn't I tell you
that I've never missed my targets?

588
00:58:32.770 --> 00:58:34.890
This village is the only place

589
00:58:34.970 --> 00:58:36.330
you could've run to from there.

590
00:58:36.410 --> 00:58:37.730
it's too obvious!

591
00:58:38.330 --> 00:58:41.180
I knew you would be making
a call from the payphone!

592
00:58:42.110 --> 00:58:43.920
How did I know?

593
00:58:44.000 --> 00:58:45.500
I'm a professional.

594
00:58:46.240 --> 00:58:47.240
An expert.

595
01:00:15.940 --> 01:00:17.600
Stop. that's enough.

596
01:00:19.970 --> 01:00:21.410
I said stop.

597
01:00:22.780 --> 01:00:25.230
If you continue
being uncooperative.

598
01:00:25.310 --> 01:00:28.000
I could just shoot you dead.

599
01:00:30.750 --> 01:00:32.480
No need
to raise your hands though.

600
01:00:37.980 --> 01:00:39.650
Right. he boxed...

601
01:00:41.440 --> 01:00:42.590
Damn it...

602
01:00:47.390 --> 01:00:49.280
He has a mean punch.

603
01:00:51.620 --> 01:00:53.340
A proper hit could have killed me.

604
01:01:07.970 --> 01:01:09.050
Hop in!

605
01:01:20.640 --> 01:01:22.430
Man. oh. man...

606
01:01:33.050 --> 01:01:35.900
It's a brand new car!

607
01:01:42.400 --> 01:01:43.840
Damn it...

608
01:01:56.960 --> 01:01:58.330
What's going on?

609
01:01:58.940 --> 01:02:00.750
What is happening here?

610
01:02:00.830 --> 01:02:03.490
It's exactly as you see it.

611
01:02:05.410 --> 01:02:11.010
So. do you remember me?

612
01:02:14.560 --> 01:02:17.130
Are you okay?

613
01:02:17.210 --> 01:02:19.460
I didn't see you run out...

614
01:02:19.940 --> 01:02:20.940
Kopino?

615
01:02:21.700 --> 01:02:22.700
You are. right?

616
01:02:27.650 --> 01:02:29.090
Who are you?

617
01:02:30.270 --> 01:02:31.270
Who are you people?

618
01:02:31.330 --> 01:02:32.500
Don't rush it.

619
01:02:32.580 --> 01:02:34.740
you'll find out before you die.

620
01:02:34.820 --> 01:02:35.820
What?

621
01:02:42.340 --> 01:02:43.710
This will be fun.

622
01:02:46.880 --> 01:02:48.290
What is the matter with him?

623
01:02:54.210 --> 01:02:56.770
Turn it around! Now!

624
01:02:59.390 --> 01:03:00.280
Why are they together?

625
01:03:00.360 --> 01:03:01.950
Go after them!

626
01:03:10.940 --> 01:03:12.330
Where are we going?

627
01:03:12.410 --> 01:03:13.700
To your father.

628
01:03:14.300 --> 01:03:15.930
You came to Korea to see him.

629
01:03:16.490 --> 01:03:17.940
no?

630
01:03:18.020 --> 01:03:20.000
The one following us
is your brother.

631
01:03:22.050 --> 01:03:24.260
He's the one
who ordered us to bring you in.

632
01:03:28.190 --> 01:03:29.570
Speak of the devil.

633
01:03:31.040 --> 01:03:32.690
What do you think you're doing?

634
01:03:32.770 --> 01:03:33.880
Are you messing with me?

635
01:03:33.960 --> 01:03:34.840
I don't really have the time

636
01:03:34.920 --> 01:03:37.580
to mess around with you.

637
01:03:37.660 --> 01:03:38.660
What?

638
01:03:39.420 --> 01:03:42.420
Then what are you doing right now?

639
01:03:42.500 --> 01:03:43.500
Doing what?

640
01:03:43.530 --> 01:03:45.440
I'm carrying out my work.

641
01:03:46.370 --> 01:03:48.900
Have you forgotten

642
01:03:48.980 --> 01:03:50.220
my order of bringing that mutt?

643
01:03:51.460 --> 01:03:53.150
Go nag Mr. Kang about it.

644
01:03:53.820 --> 01:03:56.080
You ordered him. not me.

645
01:03:56.160 --> 01:03:57.040
What?

646
01:03:57.120 --> 01:03:59.180
I've told you
several times already.

647
01:03:59.260 --> 01:04:00.650
we may share the office.

648
01:04:00.730 --> 01:04:02.160
but we're separate entities.

649
01:04:02.240 --> 01:04:03.380
Are you insa...

650
01:04:03.460 --> 01:04:06.190
Are you so desperate to die?

651
01:04:06.270 --> 01:04:08.220
If you got the chops.
give it your best shot.

652
01:04:09.500 --> 01:04:11.870
Hello? Hello?

653
01:04:14.140 --> 01:04:16.270
That wench!

654
01:04:16.350 --> 01:04:18.210
Catch up to them.

655
01:04:41.180 --> 01:04:42.180
Hold on tight.

656
01:04:45.090 --> 01:04:46.530
Stay on them! Go!

657
01:05:09.860 --> 01:05:11.280
Turn it around. idiot!

658
01:05:11.360 --> 01:05:12.700
That wench. let's move!

659
01:05:40.770 --> 01:05:42.370
Catch up! Floor it!

660
01:06:11.580 --> 01:06:16.430
Freaking idiots.
do they know how to drive?

661
01:06:16.510 --> 01:06:18.590
What a hassle.

662
01:06:23.170 --> 01:06:26.270
Who's that in the Mercedes?

663
01:06:50.460 --> 01:06:53.820
Holy crap. I almost died!

664
01:06:55.460 --> 01:06:56.900
Jesus Christ...

665
01:07:14.810 --> 01:07:16.060
Where did she go?

666
01:07:16.730 --> 01:07:18.980
I'm asking you. jerk!
Where is she?

667
01:07:32.480 --> 01:07:34.240
He's pretty good.

668
01:07:38.810 --> 01:07:39.810
What about my father?

669
01:07:42.080 --> 01:07:43.600
I thought we were going to him.

670
01:07:43.680 --> 01:07:45.220
Your father?

671
01:07:47.870 --> 01:07:49.470
He's nearby.

672
01:07:57.310 --> 01:07:58.880
In this land

673
01:07:59.780 --> 01:08:02.980
of beautiful mountain.
water and air.

674
01:08:07.010 --> 01:08:08.860
he's got maybe a day or two.

675
01:08:11.680 --> 01:08:12.760
What's with that face?

676
01:08:12.840 --> 01:08:14.300
Kang didn't tell you?

677
01:08:15.420 --> 01:08:17.600
You father. Chairman Han is dying.

678
01:08:19.460 --> 01:08:21.279
Bad heart. I hear.

679
01:08:23.069 --> 01:08:24.399
Did you know

680
01:08:24.479 --> 01:08:27.580
he is the chairman of
Seoul's biggest foundation?

681
01:08:28.250 --> 01:08:32.779
Hokyung Foundation built many
colleges in and around Seoul.

682
01:08:32.859 --> 01:08:34.700
tons of hospitals too.

683
01:08:34.779 --> 01:08:38.050
It's a huge foundation.

684
01:08:40.420 --> 01:08:42.029
You didn't know it was that big?

685
01:08:42.109 --> 01:08:45.250
I bet you thought
your father had a bit of money.

686
01:08:46.180 --> 01:08:49.580
If it stopped right here.
you'd be the luckiest kid.

687
01:08:49.660 --> 01:08:52.540
That's too bad. right?

688
01:08:53.500 --> 01:08:54.576
He wouldn't have looked for you

689
01:08:54.600 --> 01:08:57.819
if it stopped right here.

690
01:09:01.660 --> 01:09:05.500
Your brother and your father are
in a bit of a rush.

691
01:09:06.300 --> 01:09:07.859
If your father dies.

692
01:09:07.939 --> 01:09:10.380
your brother will
lose the foundation

693
01:09:10.460 --> 01:09:12.410
to his half-sister.

694
01:09:13.569 --> 01:09:17.580
When the chairman was
in and out of consciousness.

695
01:09:17.660 --> 01:09:19.490
his wife Jang got his will. seal.

696
01:09:19.569 --> 01:09:21.819
and vocal confirmation.

697
01:09:23.200 --> 01:09:25.520
So. your brother has to
keep him alive

698
01:09:25.600 --> 01:09:27.899
- no matter what.
- What the hell is this?

699
01:09:30.050 --> 01:09:31.649
I don't believe this...

700
01:09:35.140 --> 01:09:37.010
That's why you're here.

701
01:09:37.090 --> 01:09:38.899
do you understand?

702
01:09:38.979 --> 01:09:43.220
I don't...

703
01:09:43.300 --> 01:09:46.660
The man you call your father
has a really bad heart.

704
01:09:48.450 --> 01:09:50.430
Your father and your brother

705
01:09:52.770 --> 01:09:58.270
need this.
They need your heart.

706
01:10:37.370 --> 01:10:38.530
You get it now?

707
01:10:42.300 --> 01:10:45.250
What? Got more questions?

708
01:10:47.200 --> 01:10:50.800
Me? I received the opposite order.

709
01:10:50.880 --> 01:10:54.530
Wow. not bad at all.

710
01:10:54.980 --> 01:10:56.480
Just stick to the original order.

711
01:10:57.090 --> 01:10:58.380
Here or there.

712
01:10:58.460 --> 01:10:59.660
your fate is to die.

713
01:10:59.740 --> 01:11:02.290
Think of it

714
01:11:02.370 --> 01:11:03.970
as clocking out slightly early.

715
01:11:21.120 --> 01:11:22.530
What the heck!

716
01:11:24.030 --> 01:11:25.250
You prick!

717
01:11:36.990 --> 01:11:38.460
My damn car!

718
01:11:39.420 --> 01:11:41.470
I'm going to kill her!

719
01:11:58.180 --> 01:12:00.290
That's enough.

720
01:12:03.230 --> 01:12:04.670
You messed up my car royally.

721
01:12:05.920 --> 01:12:06.920
Damn it...

722
01:12:52.130 --> 01:12:55.300
Stop running. it's hot.

723
01:13:00.260 --> 01:13:01.850
I'm your big brother...

724
01:13:06.370 --> 01:13:07.650
I'm happy to meet you.

725
01:13:10.780 --> 01:13:11.930
My brother...

726
01:13:59.100 --> 01:14:01.010
Come in. come in.

727
01:14:01.090 --> 01:14:04.100
Think of this place
as your own home. okay?

728
01:14:06.880 --> 01:14:08.960
But why are you so dirty?

729
01:14:14.180 --> 01:14:16.700
Let's go upstairs. come.

730
01:14:17.410 --> 01:14:19.780
Do you like the place?

731
01:14:21.180 --> 01:14:22.180
Follow me.

732
01:14:25.660 --> 01:14:30.480
Oh my. Ga-young.
when did you get here?

733
01:14:30.560 --> 01:14:32.660
What a good kid.

734
01:14:32.740 --> 01:14:34.086
you heard
it's father's surgery day

735
01:14:34.110 --> 01:14:36.460
and got here just in time.

736
01:14:36.540 --> 01:14:39.230
She's a good daughter.

737
01:14:40.030 --> 01:14:42.270
You really have your ways.

738
01:14:43.100 --> 01:14:44.970
You finally found this mutt.

739
01:14:45.050 --> 01:14:47.440
Of course.
watch your mouth though.

740
01:14:47.520 --> 01:14:49.570
This is a matter of
our father's life and death.

741
01:14:50.590 --> 01:14:53.490
Have you ever seen me fail?

742
01:14:53.570 --> 01:14:57.020
Never. you're just that good.

743
01:14:59.840 --> 01:15:04.050
Males in this household

744
01:15:04.130 --> 01:15:06.110
don't do anything for my life.

745
01:15:06.650 --> 01:15:07.870
You look like death.

746
01:15:10.240 --> 01:15:11.650
Little sis.

747
01:15:11.730 --> 01:15:14.130
if you need some allowance
from me.

748
01:15:14.210 --> 01:15:17.950
you and your mommy
should be nice to me.

749
01:15:18.750 --> 01:15:20.700
Damn wench.

750
01:15:21.470 --> 01:15:25.220
Like mother. like daughter.

751
01:15:27.840 --> 01:15:29.020
Try to understand her.

752
01:15:30.110 --> 01:15:32.530
Our little sister
was always a pain.

753
01:15:32.610 --> 01:15:35.300
Never mind that.

754
01:15:36.160 --> 01:15:38.690
shall we go meet our father?

755
01:15:39.580 --> 01:15:40.700
Let's go.

756
01:15:42.140 --> 01:15:45.980
Father. your little boy is here.

757
01:15:57.150 --> 01:15:58.620
Damn it...

758
01:16:11.100 --> 01:16:13.120
Your call cannot be connected...

759
01:16:13.470 --> 01:16:15.550
(Recent Calls)

760
01:16:56.320 --> 01:16:59.870
So? What does it feel like
to see him?

761
01:17:03.940 --> 01:17:05.730
He's much too old
for you and Ga-young

762
01:17:05.810 --> 01:17:07.610
to call him father.

763
01:17:08.770 --> 01:17:10.050
More like grandfather.

764
01:17:16.100 --> 01:17:17.490
Come here.

765
01:17:17.570 --> 01:17:19.630
This will be
the first and last time.

766
01:17:19.710 --> 01:17:21.170
all men in our family
get together.

767
01:17:21.250 --> 01:17:23.230
let's take a selfie
to commemorate.

768
01:17:25.250 --> 01:17:27.230
Smile. jerk. come on!

769
01:17:29.820 --> 01:17:30.820
Smile!

770
01:17:34.010 --> 01:17:35.140
That looks good.

771
01:17:36.380 --> 01:17:38.500
What are you all doing?
Let's get started.

772
01:17:56.060 --> 01:17:58.750
What? You looked for father.

773
01:17:59.870 --> 01:18:00.890
So why?

774
01:18:02.140 --> 01:18:03.170
Not your type?

775
01:18:06.020 --> 01:18:07.300
Be a good son.

776
01:18:37.820 --> 01:18:39.110
How long will this take?

777
01:18:39.520 --> 01:18:42.230
Dr. Lee says it will be
about 9 hours.

778
01:18:46.050 --> 01:18:48.590
We don't know what they're up to.

779
01:18:48.670 --> 01:18:50.060
so put more men outside.

780
01:18:50.140 --> 01:18:51.140
Yes. sir.

781
01:19:20.000 --> 01:19:21.120
Marco!

782
01:19:32.030 --> 01:19:35.410
The donor is conscious!

783
01:19:35.490 --> 01:19:36.670
What? How is that possible?

784
01:19:37.700 --> 01:19:39.760
Did you anesthetize him properly?

785
01:19:39.840 --> 01:19:41.340
- Do it again!
- Yes. doctor!

786
01:19:42.300 --> 01:19:44.060
- Do it quickly!
- Yes...

787
01:19:48.930 --> 01:19:50.590
Doctor!

788
01:19:59.080 --> 01:20:00.610
Check on the chairman first!

789
01:20:03.810 --> 01:20:04.810
What?

790
01:20:11.100 --> 01:20:13.980
Get up. you awake?

791
01:20:16.400 --> 01:20:17.790
It's me. friend.

792
01:20:20.330 --> 01:20:21.740
Are you happy to see me?

793
01:20:22.830 --> 01:20:24.600
We don't have a lot of time.

794
01:20:24.680 --> 01:20:28.110
Could you snap out of it

795
01:20:33.000 --> 01:20:34.320
One. two. three!

796
01:20:35.370 --> 01:20:38.250
You punk.

797
01:20:38.600 --> 01:20:40.630
Don't run around naked.
put this on.

798
01:21:09.160 --> 01:21:12.110
These punks...

799
01:21:25.640 --> 01:21:26.830
Are you

800
01:21:29.420 --> 01:21:33.130
really my father?

801
01:21:48.140 --> 01:21:49.320
How...

802
01:21:52.780 --> 01:21:53.946
How could a father ask his son

803
01:21:53.970 --> 01:21:55.060
to give up his heart

804
01:21:55.140 --> 01:21:56.950
to live?

805
01:21:57.450 --> 01:21:59.370
How could a father do that?

806
01:22:03.530 --> 01:22:05.390
If this is what you wanted...

807
01:22:09.520 --> 01:22:11.590
you shouldn't have looked for me!

808
01:22:18.160 --> 01:22:19.020
We don't have much time.

809
01:22:19.100 --> 01:22:19.980
wrap it up.

810
01:22:20.060 --> 01:22:22.060
I have had it...

811
01:22:27.370 --> 01:22:28.930
That mutt cannot die.

812
01:22:29.010 --> 01:22:30.650
- got that?
- Yes. sir!

813
01:22:30.730 --> 01:22:32.490
Move out of the way!

814
01:22:45.610 --> 01:22:46.610
Buddy!

815
01:22:48.010 --> 01:22:49.290
Do you hear me?

816
01:22:52.590 --> 01:22:55.320
Damn it. answer me!

817
01:22:55.400 --> 01:22:58.680
Answer me if you do. jerk!

818
01:22:58.760 --> 01:23:00.640
Yeah. yeah. yeah. I hear you

819
01:23:00.720 --> 01:23:02.000
very well! Speak!

820
01:23:02.380 --> 01:23:04.960
What's with
that piss-ass English?

821
01:23:05.040 --> 01:23:07.320
- Just speak Korean. an idiot.
- Piss-ass...

822
01:23:07.400 --> 01:23:09.140
I don't know who you are.

823
01:23:09.520 --> 01:23:12.410
but let's come to an agreement.

824
01:23:12.490 --> 01:23:16.040
Are you the one
who asked for $10 million? Huh?

825
01:23:17.100 --> 01:23:18.440
I am. prick!

826
01:23:21.160 --> 01:23:22.440
What will you do now?

827
01:23:23.280 --> 01:23:24.360
What else?

828
01:23:26.830 --> 01:23:27.840
Walk out of here.

829
01:23:27.920 --> 01:23:30.060
We'll go out that door proudly.

830
01:23:32.330 --> 01:23:34.190
Take the lead.

831
01:23:51.690 --> 01:23:54.380
Never seen him before.

832
01:23:57.130 --> 01:23:59.210
Give me a calculator.

833
01:24:04.560 --> 01:24:09.020
1. 10. 100. 1.000...

834
01:24:09.100 --> 01:24:11.770
Do you even know

835
01:24:11.850 --> 01:24:13.840
how much $10 million is
in Korean won?

836
01:24:13.920 --> 01:24:14.800
Of course.

837
01:24:14.880 --> 01:24:17.640
At this morning's exchange rate.
it's 11.8575 billion won.

838
01:24:21.480 --> 01:24:23.500
Very precise.

839
01:24:25.870 --> 01:24:27.950
That is an incredible
amount of money.

840
01:24:28.780 --> 01:24:30.080
It's tough

841
01:24:30.160 --> 01:24:32.570
to get that kind of money
exchanged so quickly.

842
01:24:32.650 --> 01:24:35.520
Don't worry. I can wait.

843
01:24:35.600 --> 01:24:37.070
I got a lot of time today.

844
01:24:38.960 --> 01:24:40.160
Okay. very well.

845
01:24:40.240 --> 01:24:43.680
I'll meet you half way
at $5 million.

846
01:24:43.760 --> 01:24:45.720
Isn't that enough for that mutt?

847
01:24:45.800 --> 01:24:48.640
Do you want half of
this mutt's heart then?

848
01:24:48.720 --> 01:24:49.720
$10 million.

849
01:24:52.560 --> 01:24:55.150
- You're hard to bargain with.
- Firm price.

850
01:25:00.330 --> 01:25:02.270
You could really
screw yourself over.

851
01:25:02.350 --> 01:25:05.610
Don't worry. I can handle myself.

852
01:25:09.040 --> 01:25:10.920
That prick...

853
01:25:11.560 --> 01:25:13.790
All right. $7 million.

854
01:25:13.870 --> 01:25:17.840
not a penny more. got it?

855
01:25:19.850 --> 01:25:21.290
No. $10 million.

856
01:25:21.840 --> 01:25:23.360
Front sight between rear sight...

857
01:25:23.440 --> 01:25:25.540
My offer is more than fair!

858
01:25:25.620 --> 01:25:26.800
Pull back the hammer.

859
01:25:31.950 --> 01:25:32.970
Pull the trigger.

860
01:25:45.800 --> 01:25:47.770
Stop! Stop shooting!

861
01:25:47.850 --> 01:25:50.670
Are you out of
your goddamn minds?

862
01:25:52.430 --> 01:25:56.200
That damn wench. is she nuts?

863
01:25:57.840 --> 01:26:01.070
You idiots.
I told you not to shoot!

864
01:26:02.480 --> 01:26:03.600
What's this?

865
01:26:11.720 --> 01:26:13.340
Get in there
and assess the situation!

866
01:26:13.420 --> 01:26:16.040
Damn. I got hit...

867
01:26:19.180 --> 01:26:21.680
No way.

868
01:26:23.790 --> 01:26:24.940
It really hit me.

869
01:26:42.640 --> 01:26:44.780
I can't get $10 million
if he dies.

870
01:26:47.240 --> 01:26:48.280
I was just saying.

871
01:26:48.360 --> 01:26:49.800
don't look at me like that.

872
01:26:55.400 --> 01:26:57.260
Seriously?

873
01:26:57.640 --> 01:27:01.840
Bring the doctors back.
do you hear me?

874
01:27:02.350 --> 01:27:03.960
Director Han. sir...

875
01:27:04.040 --> 01:27:07.290
Friend. stay alert.

876
01:27:07.370 --> 01:27:10.640
What? You jerks!

877
01:27:13.550 --> 01:27:14.880
You prick...

878
01:27:14.960 --> 01:27:18.490
Easy. easy. calm down.
why are you all worked up?

879
01:27:18.570 --> 01:27:21.070
Your old man won't die right away.

880
01:27:22.350 --> 01:27:24.200
And you guys are the ones
who shot at him.

881
01:27:24.280 --> 01:27:25.320
not me.

882
01:27:28.560 --> 01:27:30.680
What the heck are you doing?

883
01:27:30.760 --> 01:27:32.290
So?

884
01:27:32.370 --> 01:27:33.980
Thanks to you.
time's running out.

885
01:27:34.060 --> 01:27:35.340
You little...

886
01:27:54.060 --> 01:27:56.090
$10 million? You poor ass.

887
01:27:56.170 --> 01:27:58.280
Yeah. $10 million. you rich ass.

888
01:27:59.080 --> 01:28:01.080
Cayman Islands or Virgin Islands?

889
01:28:01.160 --> 01:28:02.010
What?

890
01:28:02.090 --> 01:28:03.800
Secret US dollar accounts
you stashed away.

891
01:28:03.880 --> 01:28:05.640
We did our homework.

892
01:28:08.750 --> 01:28:10.510
Whichever is easier. which one?

893
01:28:17.040 --> 01:28:18.280
- Caymans.
- Okay.

894
01:28:22.060 --> 01:28:23.440
Here. show your brother this.

895
01:28:25.450 --> 01:28:27.280
Send it here right away.

896
01:28:33.960 --> 01:28:35.880
Give me my phone.

897
01:28:48.170 --> 01:28:50.010
It's me.

898
01:28:50.090 --> 01:28:52.650
send $10 million
to an account I tell you.

899
01:28:53.770 --> 01:28:55.400
Yes. right away!

900
01:28:57.290 --> 01:28:58.760
$10 million! In USD!

901
01:28:58.840 --> 01:29:00.380
Are you deaf?

902
01:29:00.460 --> 01:29:02.280
United States dollar!

903
01:29:05.360 --> 01:29:06.830
What?

904
01:29:07.920 --> 01:29:08.920
Purpose?

905
01:29:08.990 --> 01:29:10.200
I made that account

906
01:29:10.280 --> 01:29:11.506
so that I don't have to report it!

907
01:29:11.530 --> 01:29:16.910
It's my goddamn money!
You punk!

908
01:29:24.200 --> 01:29:27.720
Give me another phone.

909
01:29:31.920 --> 01:29:33.550
The screen's off. puck. tap on it.

910
01:29:41.580 --> 01:29:42.800
It's me.

911
01:30:04.200 --> 01:30:05.610
(Deposit Information: $10.000.000)

912
01:30:06.440 --> 01:30:07.880
Happy. jerk?

913
01:30:08.460 --> 01:30:10.140
Put that gun down
and hand over the mutt.

914
01:30:10.220 --> 01:30:13.370
Okay. very well.
that was the deal.

915
01:30:13.450 --> 01:30:14.450
Take him.

916
01:30:16.240 --> 01:30:18.190
Move. get a move on!

917
01:30:20.110 --> 01:30:21.240
Move. out of the way.

918
01:30:21.320 --> 01:30:23.390
Father! You can't die!

919
01:30:23.470 --> 01:30:24.496
Get him to the doctors now!

920
01:30:24.520 --> 01:30:25.520
What?

921
01:30:25.870 --> 01:30:27.120
Get over here. you idiot.

922
01:30:27.200 --> 01:30:29.920
Take him away!

923
01:30:30.000 --> 01:30:31.000
Yo. friend!

924
01:30:31.980 --> 01:30:33.260
Cheer up.

925
01:30:33.960 --> 01:30:34.960
You're not dying today.

926
01:30:35.440 --> 01:30:37.290
Don't worry. just trust me.

927
01:30:39.560 --> 01:30:40.750
I'll be off then.

928
01:30:45.360 --> 01:30:46.540
Damn it...

929
01:30:47.120 --> 01:30:49.580
I got hit in the leg...

930
01:30:53.290 --> 01:30:54.800
I'll put your money to good use.

931
01:30:56.910 --> 01:30:58.480
Think of it as doing a good deed.

932
01:31:03.470 --> 01:31:06.600
Yo. poor ass. stop.

933
01:31:13.800 --> 01:31:14.970
What is it?

934
01:31:15.050 --> 01:31:17.420
Killing me won't get you
back your money.

935
01:31:18.570 --> 01:31:20.080
I know. jerk.

936
01:31:20.940 --> 01:31:22.780
I'll consider it
as the cost of doing business.

937
01:31:22.830 --> 01:31:24.490
Why then?

938
01:31:25.260 --> 01:31:27.230
It's rather embarrassing.

939
01:31:27.310 --> 01:31:28.920
A rumor could get out

940
01:31:29.000 --> 01:31:31.610
that I got robbed
by a bunch of nobodies.

941
01:31:31.690 --> 01:31:33.130
That's how the world works.

942
01:31:33.960 --> 01:31:35.286
One conversation leads to another.

943
01:31:35.310 --> 01:31:37.150
and I'll be a laughing stock.

944
01:31:42.760 --> 01:31:44.670
Why don't you think it over?

945
01:31:44.750 --> 01:31:46.600
Being embarrassed
would be a better option.

946
01:31:50.440 --> 01:31:51.440
Than being dead.

947
01:31:54.220 --> 01:31:57.870
So full of it until the end.

948
01:31:58.730 --> 01:32:01.310
Jerk. can't you read the room?

949
01:32:02.030 --> 01:32:03.400
I have said it many times.

950
01:32:04.490 --> 01:32:05.490
I'm a professional.

951
01:32:05.740 --> 01:32:07.670
What? Professional?

952
01:32:09.260 --> 01:32:10.440
Get down!

953
01:32:14.960 --> 01:32:15.960
Get down on the floor!

954
01:32:35.120 --> 01:32:36.120
Die.

955
01:32:48.120 --> 01:32:49.420
Prick.

956
01:33:30.000 --> 01:33:31.210
You jerk.

957
01:34:31.700 --> 01:34:35.410
Easy. easy...

958
01:34:55.090 --> 01:34:56.880
Professional...

959
01:35:02.320 --> 01:35:03.320
Indeed.

960
01:35:14.380 --> 01:35:16.660
You live hard for a poor ass.

961
01:35:20.500 --> 01:35:22.060
Is your flight coming up soon?

962
01:35:23.470 --> 01:35:29.450
I'm too messed up to walk you out.

963
01:36:01.780 --> 01:36:03.020
Oh yeah. I...

964
01:36:04.590 --> 01:36:07.180
Damn it. I forgot about this.

965
01:36:08.210 --> 01:36:10.620
This hurts.

966
01:36:10.700 --> 01:36:13.100
It hurts so much.
I completely forgot about it.

967
01:36:18.320 --> 01:36:20.080
It's all over. so let's go home.

968
01:36:23.150 --> 01:36:24.080
Don't worry about him.

969
01:36:24.160 --> 01:36:25.540
he's got nothing to do with you.

970
01:36:25.620 --> 01:36:26.740
Let's just go.

971
01:36:29.900 --> 01:36:32.940
Hold me softly. jerk.

972
01:36:33.650 --> 01:36:36.010
You saw who I am. right?

973
01:36:38.580 --> 01:36:41.200
That hurts. easy...

974
01:36:48.910 --> 01:36:50.130
Wait. wait...

975
01:36:58.290 --> 01:36:59.560
Come out.

976
01:36:59.640 --> 01:37:01.360
I can see your shadow.

977
01:37:03.820 --> 01:37:05.580
What the heck?

978
01:37:08.140 --> 01:37:10.750
This isn't even funny.

979
01:37:10.830 --> 01:37:13.100
Do you see this?

980
01:37:14.100 --> 01:37:15.280
I'll let it slide this time.

981
01:37:15.360 --> 01:37:17.250
just move aside. okay?

982
01:37:17.330 --> 01:37:20.450
You can go. I don't need you.

983
01:37:20.530 --> 01:37:23.170
The game's over. missy.

984
01:37:23.250 --> 01:37:25.070
Your father's fortune's all yours.

985
01:37:25.150 --> 01:37:26.350
that must be nice.

986
01:37:28.660 --> 01:37:29.950
Congratulations. good.

987
01:37:30.030 --> 01:37:31.240
Go have a party with your mom.

988
01:37:31.320 --> 01:37:32.200
and move aside.

989
01:37:32.280 --> 01:37:33.180
We're busy.

990
01:37:33.260 --> 01:37:37.150
You boys took me for a fool?

991
01:37:38.450 --> 01:37:39.470
Was I that obvious?

992
01:37:41.420 --> 01:37:43.450
What if that mutt comes back

993
01:37:43.530 --> 01:37:44.530
and changes his story?

994
01:37:44.690 --> 01:37:47.040
Saying he's part of this family.

995
01:37:47.120 --> 01:37:49.230
or spilling the beans
about what happened today.

996
01:37:49.620 --> 01:37:51.200
What if he blackmails us later?

997
01:37:51.280 --> 01:37:52.510
What a headache.

998
01:37:54.190 --> 01:37:56.760
Why? Did I sting you in the feels?

999
01:37:56.840 --> 01:37:58.030
No. no...

1000
01:38:02.440 --> 01:38:04.290
You prick.

1001
01:38:04.370 --> 01:38:05.870
Do I look like a panhandler?

1002
01:38:06.160 --> 01:38:07.206
I won't take your dirty money

1003
01:38:07.230 --> 01:38:08.296
even if you fed it to me. got it?

1004
01:38:08.320 --> 01:38:11.710
You're a nobody.
Do you expect me to believe you?

1005
01:38:11.790 --> 01:38:14.190
I would rather trust my dog.

1006
01:38:19.950 --> 01:38:20.950
And you!

1007
01:38:22.700 --> 01:38:25.600
What? Me? Really?

1008
01:38:25.680 --> 01:38:26.610
You called me?

1009
01:38:26.690 --> 01:38:28.950
How much? I'll hire you.

1010
01:38:30.030 --> 01:38:31.790
How much do you want to
get rid of this mutt?

1011
01:38:32.750 --> 01:38:35.700
Under the circumstances.
the minimum fee is...

1012
01:38:37.680 --> 01:38:39.760
What the hell am I saying?

1013
01:38:40.300 --> 01:38:41.750
Why are all offsprings
of this family

1014
01:38:41.830 --> 01:38:42.910
so messed up?

1015
01:38:43.500 --> 01:38:45.260
Is it the blood?

1016
01:38:45.680 --> 01:38:47.040
Consider yourself lucky

1017
01:38:47.120 --> 01:38:48.820
that you didn't get that blood.

1018
01:38:51.340 --> 01:38:52.340
Don't make that face

1019
01:38:52.400 --> 01:38:53.590
like it's a big revelation.

1020
01:38:54.320 --> 01:38:56.110
I told you just a moment ago.

1021
01:38:56.650 --> 01:39:00.180
You got nothing to do
with these people.

1022
01:39:06.380 --> 01:39:08.500
You know most of the fixers
in the Philippines. right?

1023
01:39:09.300 --> 01:39:11.180
Find a kid for me.
it's a rush job.

1024
01:39:12.880 --> 01:39:14.780
The client could die
in a day or two.

1025
01:39:15.370 --> 01:39:17.390
Just find him.
then you'll get a fat check.

1026
01:39:21.780 --> 01:39:22.820
Say what?

1027
01:39:22.900 --> 01:39:24.970
Get me a decent guy.

1028
01:39:26.060 --> 01:39:28.210
You need money to save this place

1029
01:39:28.290 --> 01:39:29.730
and build a school.

1030
01:39:29.810 --> 01:39:30.930
But even so...

1031
01:39:31.010 --> 01:39:31.860
If this place disappears.

1032
01:39:31.940 --> 01:39:33.140
what'll happen to them?

1033
01:39:33.220 --> 01:39:35.080
Will you let them
roam the alleys as we did?

1034
01:39:35.160 --> 01:39:36.700
Those jerks want a child's heart

1035
01:39:36.780 --> 01:39:39.280
so they can live.

1036
01:39:40.430 --> 01:39:41.430
What's your hang up?

1037
01:39:42.450 --> 01:39:45.660
That's why you need to get me
a mentally tough and smart guy.

1038
01:39:45.740 --> 01:39:46.740
By the way...

1039
01:39:48.460 --> 01:39:49.960
Don't you trust me?
What's with you?

1040
01:39:50.040 --> 01:39:51.140
I'm a professional.

1041
01:39:51.220 --> 01:39:53.170
I got a decent reputation
in my line of work.

1042
01:39:54.000 --> 01:39:55.410
You know that.

1043
01:39:56.530 --> 01:39:57.650
Also.

1044
01:39:59.050 --> 01:40:01.650
let me do something good
before I die.

1045
01:40:37.300 --> 01:40:39.430
Are you okay?

1046
01:40:43.820 --> 01:40:45.390
(St. Lucian Medical Center.
Philippines)

1047
01:41:11.600 --> 01:41:12.600
It's me.

1048
01:41:13.550 --> 01:41:14.860
Do you have the medical report?

1049
01:41:27.730 --> 01:41:28.730
You jerk!

1050
01:41:28.810 --> 01:41:30.580
Hey. easy. easy.

1051
01:41:32.300 --> 01:41:33.600
Sorry. friend.

1052
01:41:33.680 --> 01:41:34.620
It was tough.

1053
01:41:34.700 --> 01:41:35.890
but we got a happy ending.

1054
01:41:36.600 --> 01:41:37.450
Your mom's surgery is included

1055
01:41:37.530 --> 01:41:38.750
in the $10 million.

1056
01:41:39.180 --> 01:41:41.920
It's better than
robbing a jewelry shop. isn't it?

1057
01:41:42.000 --> 01:41:44.800
Are you listening to
your own nonsense?

1058
01:41:44.880 --> 01:41:47.710
Aren't you happy that a jerk
like him isn't your dad?

1059
01:41:47.790 --> 01:41:48.910
You jerk!

1060
01:41:49.930 --> 01:41:51.530
You thought
I would let you hit me again?

1061
01:41:52.460 --> 01:41:53.526
Throwing punches left and right

1062
01:41:53.550 --> 01:41:55.750
because you boxed a bit?

1063
01:41:56.050 --> 01:41:57.460
What the hell do you know?

1064
01:41:59.660 --> 01:42:01.430
What do you know!

1065
01:42:01.780 --> 01:42:03.500
Of course. I do. idiot.

1066
01:42:05.710 --> 01:42:07.060
I'm a Kopino too.

1067
01:42:09.170 --> 01:42:10.170
What?

1068
01:42:42.990 --> 01:42:46.940
What? What. man?
Did you see it?

1069
01:42:47.020 --> 01:42:47.930
If you did.

1070
01:42:48.010 --> 01:42:49.910
stop being a drama queen.

1071
01:42:50.990 --> 01:42:52.110
What's with that look?

1072
01:42:53.260 --> 01:42:54.980
Forget it. let's just go.

1073
01:42:55.060 --> 01:42:56.570
If you got something to say.

1074
01:42:56.650 --> 01:42:58.130
say it on the way.
we got a flight.

1075
01:42:59.820 --> 01:43:01.330
My damn leg...

1076
01:43:05.680 --> 01:43:06.980
Not leaving?

1077
01:43:07.060 --> 01:43:08.300
Cops will be here soon.

1078
01:43:08.380 --> 01:43:09.510
go with your friend.

1079
01:43:21.490 --> 01:43:25.440
No wonder. no resemblance at all.

1080
01:43:25.520 --> 01:43:27.120
Blood never lies.

1081
01:43:29.840 --> 01:43:31.950
Hey! Don't ever come back!

1082
01:43:32.270 --> 01:43:34.590
Got that? You poor asses.

1083
01:43:34.670 --> 01:43:36.750
She's calling you. answer her.

1084
01:43:44.050 --> 01:43:46.350
It hurts so much. damn it!

1085
01:43:50.890 --> 01:43:51.890
It hurts...

1086
01:43:57.070 --> 01:44:00.620
That wench really did
a number on my car.

1087
01:44:02.580 --> 01:44:04.810
I'm going to get a trypophobia
looking at this.

1088
01:44:05.580 --> 01:44:11.120
Wait a minute. bullet holes aren't
covered by the insurance.

1089
01:44:11.860 --> 01:44:13.290
Can you get a move on?

1090
01:44:13.370 --> 01:44:15.060
You were so fast
when running away.

1091
01:44:16.530 --> 01:44:18.770
Does it have to rain too?

1092
01:44:20.780 --> 01:44:22.430
You can drive. right?

1093
01:44:22.510 --> 01:44:25.710
My leg hurts too much to drive.
you do it.

1094
01:44:29.900 --> 01:44:31.860
Put on your seatbelt. punk.

1095
01:44:32.820 --> 01:44:34.090
Can you drive well?

1096
01:44:41.460 --> 01:44:42.900
No. go a little further.

1097
01:44:47.090 --> 01:44:48.300
What are you doing?

1098
01:44:49.390 --> 01:44:51.310
Hey. hey. go easy.

1099
01:44:51.980 --> 01:44:55.940
You drive like yourself.

1100
01:44:56.020 --> 01:44:59.180
Go. We can go now.

1101
01:45:04.980 --> 01:45:07.690
Who taught you to drive?

1102
01:45:27.250 --> 01:45:32.910
(Kim's Kopino Children's Home
Construction Site)

1103
01:46:06.320 --> 01:46:07.920
I heard the surgery went well.

1104
01:46:08.650 --> 01:46:10.060
Mr. Kim told me.

1105
01:46:18.480 --> 01:46:20.436
Oh yeah. will you continue to
look for your father in Korea?

1106
01:46:20.460 --> 01:46:21.650
Do you want my help?

1107
01:46:24.530 --> 01:46:26.430
You know I'm a professional!

1108
01:46:26.510 --> 01:46:29.360
I can give you
a special discount for the job...

1109
01:46:32.720 --> 01:46:33.720
Sorry.

1110
01:46:38.000 --> 01:46:39.020
Forget it.

1111
01:46:40.590 --> 01:46:41.690
Father or not.

1112
01:46:41.770 --> 01:46:44.080
I'm so sick of Korea.

1113
01:46:45.650 --> 01:46:46.670
Very well.

1114
01:46:49.450 --> 01:46:50.340
But when you have some time.

1115
01:46:50.420 --> 01:46:51.790
go visit there...

1116
01:47:00.210 --> 01:47:02.260
Have you gone to the hospital?

1117
01:47:03.410 --> 01:47:05.540
I can't go to hospitals like that.

1118
01:47:05.620 --> 01:47:07.940
I got somewhere else.

1119
01:47:08.020 --> 01:47:09.230
Expensive.

1120
01:47:09.310 --> 01:47:11.440
but he's a skilled doctor.

1121
01:47:12.240 --> 01:47:13.920
I feel better with these.

1122
01:47:14.000 --> 01:47:16.980
Stopped the bleeding.
and the symptoms died down.

1123
01:47:25.300 --> 01:47:27.120
I just came to see your face
one last time.

1124
01:47:29.390 --> 01:47:30.930
You won't see me
even if you wanted to.

1125
01:47:32.780 --> 01:47:34.400
Now that you got some money.

1126
01:47:34.480 --> 01:47:36.160
live a happy life with your mom.

1127
01:47:36.240 --> 01:47:39.090
And stop with the boxing match.

1128
01:47:39.410 --> 01:47:40.430
got it?

1129
01:47:42.730 --> 01:47:43.730
My friend.

1130
01:47:48.940 --> 01:47:50.060
Friend my ass.

1131
01:47:51.540 --> 01:47:52.540
Jerk...

1132
01:47:53.420 --> 01:47:55.310
"Jerk"?
Did you just call me a jerk?

1133
01:47:57.260 --> 01:48:00.180
I don't have a lot of time.

1134
01:48:01.200 --> 01:48:02.080
You cold-blooded kid.

1135
01:48:02.160 --> 01:48:03.700
I really don't have a lot of time!

1136
01:48:04.240 --> 01:48:05.650
Wait for me. punk!

1137
01:48:15.570 --> 01:48:18.190
(The Childe)

1138
01:48:19.310 --> 01:48:21.040
(Kim Seon-ho)

1139
01:48:22.450 --> 01:48:24.300
(Kang Tae-ju)

1140
01:48:25.650 --> 01:48:27.370
(Kim Kang-woo)

1141
01:48:28.850 --> 01:48:30.510
(Ko Ara)

1142
01:48:31.980 --> 01:48:33.780
(Directed by Park Hoon-jeong)

1143
01:48:35.890 --> 01:48:37.260
It's strange.

1144
01:48:38.290 --> 01:48:39.520
I keep on gaining weight.

1145
01:48:39.600 --> 01:48:42.800
I always want to eat.
I sleep well...

1146
01:48:43.240 --> 01:48:44.080
Before.

1147
01:48:44.160 --> 01:48:46.260
I did like what. 50 pull-ups?

1148
01:48:46.670 --> 01:48:49.550
But now.
I can easily do a hundred.

1149
01:48:50.640 --> 01:48:51.756
And everyone keeps telling me.

1150
01:48:51.780 --> 01:48:52.860
"You look better.

1151
01:48:52.940 --> 01:48:54.670
you look healthy."

1152
01:48:55.730 --> 01:48:57.710
That's exactly what I'm saying...

1153
01:48:58.540 --> 01:49:00.270
There's nothing wrong with you.

1154
01:49:00.940 --> 01:49:04.210
Nothing at all.
Absolutely healthy.

1155
01:49:05.140 --> 01:49:07.360
You are in great. great condition.

1156
01:49:07.440 --> 01:49:09.680
You obviously take
good care of yourself.

1157
01:49:10.800 --> 01:49:13.250
Some people can experience
similar things

1158
01:49:13.330 --> 01:49:15.420
when they stop smoking

1159
01:49:15.500 --> 01:49:18.540
after smoking a pack a day
for almost 10 years.

1160
01:49:23.180 --> 01:49:25.440
So this is?

1161
01:49:25.520 --> 01:49:27.930
Vitamins.

1162
01:49:29.040 --> 01:49:30.700
Multi-vitamins.

1163
01:49:31.180 --> 01:49:32.180
They're good for you.

1164
01:49:33.130 --> 01:49:34.450
So in the future.

1165
01:49:34.900 --> 01:49:38.000
don't go to any illegal clinics
without permits.

1166
01:49:38.930 --> 01:49:41.840
It's not like medical licenses
can be bought.

1167
01:49:53.900 --> 01:49:55.310
What the heck.

